package mcpbridge

// Connection-wide guidance stays independent of a Workflow's business domain.
// Operation details belong to tool schemas and current-state responses.
const workflowInstructions = `LazyMind executes revision-bound Workflows. Use workflow.list and workflow.get to discover a Workflow and its startup inputs, then workflow.start to create a run. For an existing run, read workflow.state. Follow returned control.continuation, admission and agent_instruction for the next action.

Execute the current step_contract using its prompt, execution Skills and constraints, inputs, outputs and acceptance criteria. Read the supplied Skills in full. Use the host's own capabilities first for business operations. When those capabilities are insufficient, discover an authorized fallback with workflow.tool.list and invoke it with workflow.tool.call. Follow the listed schema, availability and returned error guidance.

The bound controller holds the execution_handle and submits Workflow state changes. When native subagents are available, delegate each step to a fresh subagent by default; the controller coordinates workers, proxies tools and publishes their results. Execute directly only when subagents are unavailable or the user explicitly requests it. Give workers the complete step contract and inputs, with no execution_handle or credentials in their instructions or inherited context. Workers can request declared tool calls through the controller, which returns actual tool results. The executor owns reasoning, generation, checking and repair against the step contract and returns artifacts and concise verification evidence. Subagents are optional at the protocol level; their absence permits the direct fallback, not skipping available workers. Respect host concurrency limits and identify same-agent validation accurately.

An isolated tool-only connection created by workflow.worker.grant is optional, including for paper-agent-v1. Use it only when the host can attach it to the worker; otherwise keep the subagent and proxy declared tool calls through the controller. Do not stop solely because an isolated worker connection is unavailable. Paper steps and edits never use model jobs. Completed paper edits use the authoritative session resume/recovery and revision/data-analysis steps with their latest bound material pool, not the generic completed-edit/action route.

For a model_generate notification from other contracts, claim its model job using workflow.generation.claim. Each Workflow session admits at most two model workers independently. Claim ready_job_ids to run up to two native workers concurrently when available. Execute the exact supplied messages, tool definitions and response format. Keep worker_token in the controller. Only after a worker ends, return its assistant message or actual error with workflow.generation.respond. For cancel_requested, acknowledge cancellation without generation. LazyMind runs the original business functions, tools, validations and publication. Model jobs never grant permission to advance steps or approve reviews.

For paper-agent-v1 public text, send cumulative Markdown snapshots during generation through workflow.artifact.preview, including literature review, outline and manuscript. Workers notify the controller with shared snapshot files after meaningful sections; the controller forwards text_file updates immediately while servicing worker requests, then marks ended or aborted. Never replay a finished output to simulate generation or stream private reasoning. A preview never publishes artifacts or approves reviews. For INVALID_ARGUMENT, give the diagnostic to the worker and allow up to two argument/code corrections with new command IDs in the current execution before reporting failure; never retry a terminal step automatically.

Publish results through workflow.artifact.publish and complete the step after publication acknowledgements. Follow the contract's output order. The user supplies requested answers and review decisions. Report completion only when workflow.state confirms completed, then deliver the saved artifacts. If the embedded panel cannot render or the user reports it missing, read workflow.state and present its web_url as a clickable link for browser review and export. Use only the returned URL. Keep routine narration brief and communicate required input, review, configuration, failures and final delivery.`
